 "final_reply": "I built the keychain tag and saved it to `/lab/work/tag.solidcraft`. I looked at a top-view render of the model, and both rows of text sit inside the plate.\n\n- **Plate:** 50 × 20 mm and 2 mm thick, with a 4 mm key-ring hole on the left, centred 5.5 mm in from the edge.\n- **Text:** raised 1 mm, so the whole tag is 3 mm tall. The model is one solid.\n- **Row 1:** \"ALEX\", 8.5 mm cap height.\n- **Row 2:** \"GYM BAG\", 5.5 mm cap height.\n\nI sized the text for a 0.4 mm nozzle, but the strokes are thinner than I wanted. The built-in font has no bold face, and the sandbox wouldn't let me load a bold font file. So I made the letters larger instead. I estimate the \"ALEX\" strokes at about 1 mm and the \"GYM BAG\" strokes at about 0.7 mm. That's from font proportions, not measured on the model. \"GYM BAG\" is the weaker row. Slicing at 0.2 mm layers with a small line width should keep it clean, but check the preview before printing.\n\nI didn't export an STL or 3MF, since you only asked for the design file. The design was built in a headless session, so the SolidCraft window never showed it.",
